1
00:00:01,880 --> 00:00:04,140
The Closed tab lists the trades you have closed. It starts with the last day.

2
00:00:04,240 --> 00:00:06,860
Click the period button to look further back.

3
00:00:06,960 --> 00:00:08,610
Pick 5 Days, 1 Month or 6 Months, or Custom for your own dates.

4
00:00:08,710 --> 00:00:14,210
For Custom, type the From and Till dates.

5
00:00:14,310 --> 00:00:19,820
Click Show Result.

6
00:00:19,920 --> 00:00:23,180
Every trade closed in that range is listed.

7
00:00:23,280 --> 00:00:29,530
To add a column, right-click a heading and choose Customize.

8
00:00:29,630 --> 00:00:34,300
Tick Reason, then click Ok.

9
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:39,160
Reason shows why a trade closed, such as S for stop loss or L for take profit. A dash means you closed it.

10
00:00:39,260 --> 00:00:43,230
The arrow at the right of the status bar shows the rollover time and the clock.

11
00:00:43,330 --> 00:00:45,790
Click it again to hide them.

